    "mechanism": "Fast liquidity-state shift: a quoted spread that is suddenly wide vs its own trailing-60s distribution flags an immediate quoting stress -- market makers pulling liquidity ahead of expected adverse selection. The built-in spread_z_300s averages over five minutes and is slow to react; a 60s window catches the widening within seconds of it starting. Spread widening precedes volatility bursts and often precedes the directional move that the wider quotes are protecting against, so the fast z should lead the slow one into 15-60s returns.",
